Build succeeded. The `UserActivityTracker` component is ready. Here's how to use it:

```razor
<UserActivityTracker TimeoutSeconds="120" OnIdle="HandleIdle" OnActive="HandleActive">
    <p>Your app content here...</p>
</UserActivityTracker>

@code {
    private Task HandleIdle() { /* user went idle */ return Task.CompletedTask; }
    private Task HandleActive() { /* user is back */ return Task.CompletedTask; }
}
```

**What it does:**
- Listens for `mousemove`, `keydown`, `click`, and `scroll` on the wrapper `<div>`
- Fires `OnIdle` after `TimeoutSeconds` of inactivity (default 300)
- Fires `OnActive` when activity resumes after idle
- Cleans up all timers and event listeners on dispose via `IAsyncDisposable`
